      "unit": "U2",
      "test": "core/internal/session/spool_test.go — a spooled end whose last_seq is past the recording's last output frame, with the session no longer listed: a gap marker from the spool's numbers, then the end marker stamped ended_at"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A loss the spool reports (spool-entry.schema.json). The core recorded output 1 to 3 and was killed; while it was away the target printed 4 to 9 and orphan_timeout ended the session, and by the time the core returned the worker had lingered out and exited, taking its ring with it. The spool says last_seq 9, out_bytes 71 and the stamp of frame 9, so the core writes a gap marker before the end marker — 71 less the 23 bytes it held, from frame 3's stamp to frame 9's — and then the end marker stamped with the worker's ended_at. The recording never reads as complete when it is not (immortality §4.3). This case is graded by the core's own test alone: the spool entry is deleted once the end is written, so no collection holds the numbers an artefact check would need.",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §4.3",
    "session model §11",
    "session model §15"
  ],
